  "authored_scope": "Random scenes are 12..30 per side; explicit sizes may be 8..30. The fixtures span 14..26, so 27..30 is a synthetic extension. Each scene has 1..6 distinctly coloured rectilinear outlines. Each is the 8-neighbour boundary of a box with 0..2 corner notches and an optional middle-side bite. At least one outline is closed and filled by a strict plurality of its interior dots, with 1..4 votes for the winner. Open outlines lose a 4-connected run of 1..5 boundary cells; the run starts on a straight side and may wrap round a corner. Open outlines may hold decoy dots, and there are further distractor dots outside. Not supported: closed outlines without dots, voting ties, nested outlines, and walls that touch other walls. Fixtures are replayed through input_grid, which parses the grid rather than taking explicit latent arguments, because the fixture outlines are irregular hand-drawn shapes.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Shape bounding boxes are separated by at least one background row or column, so walls never touch.",
    "Each outline has its own colour, which differs from every other outline colour.",
    "Each wall is a single 4-connected component with at least 4 cells. It is therefore one wall under either 4- or 8-connectivity.",
    "Every dot is 8-isolated from all other dots and from wall cells of its own colour, so it stays a singleton.",
    "Closed interiors use the 8-neighbour boundary, so they are sealed under both 4- and 8-connectivity.",
    "Gaps in open outlines are seeded on a straight side, so the interior reaches the outside under 4-connectivity.",
    "A flood fill from the border checks that the set of unreached non-wall cells equals the union of the closed interiors.",
    "The winning colour in a closed interior has strictly more votes than any other colour and differs from the wall colour.",
    "Each closed interior has at least one dot, so every output differs from its input.",
    "input_grid cannot be combined with scene parameters, and explicit out-of-range or inconsistent counts raise ValueError."
  ],
